        "id": "step_hook_01",
        "title": "Investigation 1: The Hook",
        "difficulty": "Observe",
        "tensionLevel": 2,
        "prerequisites": [
          "step_baseline_00"
        ],
        "components": [
          {
            "id": "comp_hook_story",
            "type": "StoryNarrative",
            "props": {
              "episodeId": "ep_hook_01",
              "markdown": "### Investigation 1 of 9\n\n**MISSION**: Meet someone who discovered a hidden option.\n\n**YOU WILL PRODUCE**:\n● ☐ A prediction about Lethabo's choice\n\n**TIME**: 5 minutes\n**DIFFICULTY**: 🟢 Observe\n\n---\n\n### Episode 1: The Boy Who Saw a Third Option\n\nMeet Lethabo.\n\nLethabo is seventeen. He lives with his grandmother—the same grandmother who takes pills for her heart. He is the one who notices when she forgets. He is the one who reminds her. He is the one who started building clocks to help her remember.\n\nHe has R200 saved. He has been saving for months. He wants a new phone case. Nothing fancy—just something to protect his phone.\n\nThen his friends make a plan. A weekend trip to an amusement park. Entry is R150. Food is extra. If he goes, most of his savings will be gone. If he does not go, he will feel left out.\n\nHe sits on his bed, thinking.\n\nWhat are my options?\n1. Go — spend R150, have fun, but savings gone.\n2. Do not go — keep savings, feel left out.\n\nHe thinks there are only two options.\n\nThen he remembers something. A girl named Myah, from the taxi rank. She carries a notebook. She asked him once: \"What do people actually want?\"\n\nHe stops. He asks himself: \"What do my friends actually want?\"\n\nThey want to spend time together. Not the amusement park specifically. Just time together.\n\nSo he suggests something cheaper. A picnic at the park. Everyone brings food. No entry fee. Everyone can afford it.\n\nHis friends agree.\n\nHe saves his money. He keeps his friendships.\n\nThe third option did not exist until he looked for it.\n\nBut Lethabo does not feel relieved. He feels something else. He wonders if he made the right choice. He wonders if his friends secretly resent him. He wonders if he should have just spent the money.\n\nHe is seventeen. He made a good choice. But he still does not know if he can trust his own decisions.",
              "pivots": [
                {
                  "text": "Continue to Evidence Challenge",
                  "beiScore": 5
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "comp_hook_evidence_decision",
            "type": "PrivateReflection",
            "props": {
              "prompt": "🔎 Evidence Challenge\n\n\"Think of a decision you made in the last 24 hours.\"\n\n✍️ My decision:",
              "placeholder": "...",
              "isPrivate": true
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "comp_hook_evidence_perceived",
            "type": "PrivateReflection",
            "props": {
              "prompt": "✍️ My perceived options: 1.   2.",
              "placeholder": "1. ...\n2. ...",
              "isPrivate": true
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "comp_hook_evidence_hidden",
            "type": "PrivateReflection",
            "props": {
              "prompt": "✍️ The option I didn't see:",
              "placeholder": "...",
              "isPrivate": true
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "comp_hook_predict",
            "type": "StoryNarrative",
            "props": {
              "episodeId": "ep_hook_01_predict",
              "markdown": "### 🤔 Predict\n\n\"What would you have done if you were Lethabo?\"",
              "pivots": [
                {
                  "text": "Go to the amusement park and spend the money",
                  "beiScore": 1
                },
                {
                  "text": "Stay home and feel left out",
                  "beiScore": 2
                },
                {
                  "text": "Suggest something cheaper (a picnic in the park)",
                  "beiScore": 5
                },
                {
                  "text": "Borrow money to go anyway",
                  "beiScore": 3
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "comp_hook_pause",
            "type": "MindfulBreath",
            "props": {
              "inhaleSeconds": 5,
              "holdSeconds": 5,
              "exhaleSeconds": 5,
              "cycles": 2,
              "prompt": "⏸ PAUSE\n\nClose the workbook.\n\nTake 30 seconds.\n\nAsk yourself:\n\n\"What surprised me most so far?\"\n\nThen continue."
            }
          }
        ]
