          "step_prediction_02"
        ],
        "components": [
          {
            "id": "comp_rev_story",
            "type": "StoryNarrative",
            "props": {
              "episodeId": "ep_rev_03",
              "markdown": "### Investigation 3 of 9\n\n**MISSION**: Discover the hidden structure of every decision.\n\n**YOU WILL PRODUCE**:\n● ☐ Understanding of decision patterns\n● ☐ Prediction calibration check\n\n**TIME**: 3 minutes\n**DIFFICULTY**: 🟡 Analyse\n\n---\n\n### Episode 2: What Lethabo Didn't See\n\nLethabo saved his money. He kept his friendships. He made the smart choice.\n\nBut he still worries.\n\nHe worries that his friends are secretly disappointed. He worries that he should have just spent the money. He worries that he is too careful, too cautious, too afraid.\n\nHere is what nobody told him: every decision has a third option. Sometimes a fourth. Sometimes a fifth.\n\nThe question is not whether they exist. The question is whether you are willing to look for them.\n\nLethabo found his third option by asking what his friends actually wanted. He saw the need beneath the request. He did not ask: \"What can I afford?\" He asked: \"What do they actually need?\"\n\nThat is the skill.\n\nBut he still does not know if he can trust his own judgement. He still wonders if he should have just gone along with the crowd.\n\nHe is seventeen. He made a good choice. But he is still learning to trust his own decisions.\n\nThe next day, he walks past the spaza shop. He sees Sipho—the boy who fixed the radio—standing outside, holding a packet of screws. Sipho looks at him.\n\n\"You're Lethabo, right? The clock guy?\"\n\nLethabo nods.\n\n\"I'm going to build something,\" Sipho says. \"I don't know what yet. But I'm going to build it.\"\n\nLethabo does not know what to say. He just nods again.\n\nSipho walks away.\n\nLethabo stays there, wondering what Sipho is building—and wondering what he himself is building.\n\n---\n\n### 👁️ The Observer\n\n\"Interesting. Lethabo made the right choice. But he still doesn't trust himself.\"",
              "pivots": [
                {
                  "text": "Check my prediction",
                  "beiScore": 5
                }
              ]
            }
          },
